r this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7 \\\\  & ↓ & -10 \\\\  & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+7}{x+2}=5-\\frac{3}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x+7}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5-\\frac{3}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\text{d}x-3\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-49354/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49354"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49398/selection/a5221bf5219719264ce82e6834f570b4690cc4627bd43eb9432170bf0ca936cf" :answer/id #uuid "2708a6b9-fb75-5c92-9425-f57e1167c066" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49398/selection/da5694eb50a1f1fab6f1fb924dc6e6d697cdd2aa9940fb3ba4e10cde53746f40" :answer/id #uuid "c248c35d-9a92-551e-802d-626ecaaa5da8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49398/selection/2247141a4882d084b49fc49ca8e7c4f37c6adf289245947f11106ff67cf192fb" :answer/id #uuid "61f4887b-3d01-58b1-bcd9-d2fb19997842" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49398/selection/29f4127a7bc14e71aed2aec17818d2d20f810bcb053a2b865dbe1094ab215ab8" :answer/id #uuid "2e147fd6-0f93-5c00-8018-d07ef10f0ae8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49398/selection/bbd19215aa3aea53bc9b223673ee24a6efe765e95f8d63b0ff3f4927a5202c1a" :answer/id #uuid "8f75d583-8a2e-5cf8-a698-0af2fdc387f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49398/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "461040fd-6236-57ff-af4a-4babd622bde1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49398/selection/a5221bf5219719264ce82e6834f570b4690cc4627bd43eb9432170bf0ca936cf" :answer-field/choices ["q-49398/selection/a5221bf5219719264ce82e6834f570b4690cc4627bd43eb9432170bf0ca936cf" "q-49398/selection/da5694eb50a1f1fab6f1fb924dc6e6d697cdd2aa9940fb3ba4e10cde53746f40" "q-49398/selection/2247141a4882d084b49fc49ca8e7c4f37c6adf289245947f11106ff67cf192fb" "q-49398/selection/29f4127a7bc14e71aed2aec17818d2d20f810bcb053a2b865dbe1094ab215ab8" "q-49398/selection/bbd19215aa3aea53bc9b223673ee24a6efe765e95f8d63b0ff3f4927a5202c1a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49398" :question/id #uuid "fef7e5a4-8743-520c-8404-5503ee85f90a" :question/math-academy-id "q-49398" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{x+4}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 \\\\  & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+4}{x+3}=1+\\frac{1}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{x+4}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(1+\\frac{1}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{|}_{-2}^{0}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =(0-(-2))+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-2+3|) \\\\  & =2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-49398/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49398"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49456/selection/b613206de76175556e904bbbb11be46117dee9ca565fe03ce0380ea5d4d36322" :answer/id #uuid "66c47afb-0399-5e9b-bb15-85438050f36b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49456/selection/132b46c549f6cbe97c5ce551979b731fd429b1c8744ebb81df895804c66ef0a4" :answer/id #uuid "0dcd9336-343a-59a5-ae33-3e75a9e8f1de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-3x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49456/selection/d3ad6b20f8cb702440d39126996f44210c8747dde8d420b547fa037527262819" :answer/id #uuid "ca0308f5-8d24-5bea-8cea-4b6d5f17f3ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49456/selection/998302303144e5bd53296ec06b6f9c1e1d36fa265bf395a18d6fef8d4b625a89" :answer/id #uuid "953549fb-6843-5e38-a909-0b2d32bb2e7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49456/selection/0bb2d3e17f375fa6853d86d846e6b380cb0a5b02f613bd51cffb98ab7b038315" :answer/id #uuid "1b57d584-29e0-514d-8ce7-8bf95af333ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49456/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "06777435-7464-543f-9a23-0ac5af9f8489" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49456/selection/0bb2d3e17f375fa6853d86d846e6b380cb0a5b02f613bd51cffb98ab7b038315" :answer-field/choices ["q-49456/selection/b613206de76175556e904bbbb11be46117dee9ca565fe03ce0380ea5d4d36322" "q-49456/selection/132b46c549f6cbe97c5ce551979b731fd429b1c8744ebb81df895804c66ef0a4" "q-49456/selection/d3ad6b20f8cb702440d39126996f44210c8747dde8d420b547fa037527262819" "q-49456/selection/998302303144e5bd53296ec06b6f9c1e1d36fa265bf395a18d6fef8d4b625a89" "q-49456/selection/0bb2d3e17f375fa6853d86d846e6b380cb0a5b02f613bd51cffb98ab7b038315"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49456" :question/id #uuid "1b477fe5-67ac-5170-be29-6f6d97baa23e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49456" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 3 & 3 & -9 & 1 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & 9 & 0 & 3 \\\\  & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}=3{x}^{2}+1+\\frac{2}{x-3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+1+\\frac{2}{x-3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-49456/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49456"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347423/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "3cfbefb0-1e7d-58bd-88d6-a4c41d5a49af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347423/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4818e830-08f2-554f-9402-1d79ba7f7d3d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347423/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-347423/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347423" :question/id #uuid "5fe6f2fa-cc5e-5c73-ad78-fa9e31680504" :question/math-academy-id "q-347423" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+3x-2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $3$ | $8$ | $3$ | $-2$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-6$ | $-4$ | $2$ |\n|  | $3$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+3x-2}{x+2}=3{x}^{2}+2x-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+3x-2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3{x}^{2}+2x-1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{|}_{0}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{2}-x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}{|}_{0}^{2}+{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{2}-x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =[{2}^{3}-{0}^{3}]+[{2}^{2}-{0}^{2}]-[2-0] \\\\  & =8+4-2 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-347423/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347423"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352251/field-1/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" :answer/id #uuid "a2c5787d-d7e3-5c45-88f6-9f602635fd03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352251/field-1/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "0084de06-a6d0-541b-b334-13d2ae825c01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352251/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5699bfe5-3b47-5cd8-ba8e-9f9e32c6dbb5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352251/field-1/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" :answer-field/choices ["q-352251/field-1/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" "q-352251/field-1/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352251/field-2/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "4b253819-013c-5d7e-97cb-922d405d2e74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352251/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "51adb47e-4040-53ad-b1d8-8b01c644e36d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352251/field-2/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer-field/choices ["q-352251/field-2/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352251" :question/id #uuid "ba1ca2cd-3164-58aa-80ce-61d1bd84a956" :question/math-academy-id "q-352251" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+2x+5}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,\\,5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-2$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+2x+5}{x+2}={x}^{2}+x+\\frac{5}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+2x+5}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+x+\\frac{5}{x+2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x+5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}+5(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{3}{2}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352251/field-1" "q-352251/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352251"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114879/selection/6f99701bc7474e906db6329391ca708f70e1935b39bd10aadbae73eae7a10a97" :answer/id #uuid "244e548b-2fb8-500f-a108-39cd456a970b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{2}-x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114879/selection/1ce09d44560d8bd252e84172fbd8e5023c347f248a129c1d293ea65ce769458f" :answer/id #uuid "f349a1f0-879b-5869-97b3-7beded281852" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{2}+x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114879/selection/6f5f6e92ac399e8484761577948e43801333464d181e9de39ecd1fced3b2e338" :answer/id #uuid "a65710fc-5e2a-5559-b79e-93861e08b34e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}-2x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114879/selection/13d7b62ca940201777984b7fae26df0381d7900d6f628bfaef6108bec36454c6" :answer/id #uuid "2fc6059b-7293-5aa3-92c7-3092e97eca56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+x+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114879/selection/abf838fe84519a39c0f49fa12765adab26699eb97b8f4fc78cd877525e5415fc" :answer/id #uuid "b52d573b-81a2-51c7-8163-7bb56f844deb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114879/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "18dffca6-b990-50d2-8e7f-2a26d9453908" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114879/selection/abf838fe84519a39c0f49fa12765adab26699eb97b8f4fc78cd877525e5415fc" :answer-field/choices ["q-114879/selection/6f99701bc7474e906db6329391ca708f70e1935b39bd10aadbae73eae7a10a97" "q-114879/selection/1ce09d44560d8bd252e84172fbd8e5023c347f248a129c1d293ea65ce769458f" "q-114879/selection/6f5f6e92ac399e8484761577948e43801333464d181e9de39ecd1fced3b2e338" "q-114879/selection/13d7b62ca940201777984b7fae26df0381d7900d6f628bfaef6108bec36454c6" "q-114879/selection/abf838fe84519a39c0f49fa12765adab26699eb97b8f4fc78cd877525e5415fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114879" :question/id #uuid "203b8faf-aa8f-5bc8-8c68-2ac25460b3aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-114879" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x+1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & 3 & 1 \\\\  & 3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x+1}{x-1}=3x+1+\\frac{2}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}-2x+1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3x+1+\\frac{2}{x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114879/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114879"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-49421/selection/d732578a490ffce9a8c65accae6b1aa2ee0b2acaea7488b0b18aad35cf400e99" :answer/id #uuid "25598e22-6f0a-5255-920d-f516cc74ae91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+9x-16\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49421/selection/b57b9384495195ff2cf1c1b6ea1a4d066ade58e3594936a8de0da302122778bc" :answer/id #uuid "84763b15-40f1-5825-b82e-26fe15468bb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+3x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49421/selection/a0acd20b5fd45ecb36524c3089e24ea3169c4b2e427512a7612fe58d690036e1" :answer/id #uuid "5426e042-f327-5f9f-ac58-a808fb35adb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49421/selection/0d6dfd8d86e2e59102c10e729ddc635ba158facb2d15d7ea80992afb0d6ea321" :answer/id #uuid "40cfe201-9787-508c-8e70-b0596683b0da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49421/selection/970e685e6ff28a473c72230e89645cef0760680be86bf15103d7a9ead9d80faa" :answer/id #uuid "1ba9139d-9490-5d2b-8385-69b3e7d3faab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49421/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0524d15-486e-578f-914b-d6f592515942" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49421/selection/d732578a490ffce9a8c65accae6b1aa2ee0b2acaea7488b0b18aad35cf400e99" :answer-field/choices ["q-49421/selection/d732578a490ffce9a8c65accae6b1aa2ee0b2acaea7488b0b18aad35cf400e99" "q-49421/selection/b57b9384495195ff2cf1c1b6ea1a4d066ade58e3594936a8de0da302122778bc" "q-49421/selection/a0acd20b5fd45ecb36524c3089e24ea3169c4b2e427512a7612fe58d690036e1" "q-49421/selection/0d6dfd8d86e2e59102c10e729ddc635ba158facb2d15d7ea80992afb0d6ea321" "q-49421/selection/970e685e6ff28a473c72230e89645cef0760680be86bf15103d7a9ead9d80faa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49421" :question/id #uuid "3542045d-f5df-5dac-bdce-4e5e5781c7c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-49421" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & -1 & 2 \\\\  & ↓ & -2 & 10 & -18 \\\\  & 1 & -5 & 9 & -16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2}{x+2}={x}^{2}-5x+9-\\frac{16}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-x+2}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}-5x+9-\\frac{16}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int x\\,\\text{d}x+9\\int \\text{d}x-16\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{2}+9x-16\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-49421/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49421"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114892/selection/d6ac097fc4be373c41b4c0395ed665d7e57a175ad636bf8133302d28472ae4b4" :answer/id #uuid "d676c07a-2c0b-5e82-8d20-961e7ff5d295" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114892/selection/bfb95ea717d59358860f0615a38c5a1c60c502b49272d182b54768de605d975b" :answer/id #uuid "b07adba2-af32-5eed-b5ee-f2a3af2eb6b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-\\frac{7}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114892/selection/0bdb3932af7cd815b3772b59b683586b1d77a12e90bdba358128ae83aa0ae167" :answer/id #uuid "0f653e82-13d0-54e1-bd07-0e39840726b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\frac{11}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114892/selection/29c33bfd6d1591d14ddbf2aba437b23e0305d7be3e8226d3b2fad41ffcbdeea8" :answer/id #uuid "a2dd0056-0de0-52ae-98b1-6e8c055fa2ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-\\frac{13}{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114892/selection/f7c1bd5baf2cded1aba0b23d3926e4ee550542bfbe6822146aeca77be444a09f" :answer/id #uuid "7f8483fc-fe41-5200-9dbe-866b108118b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3-\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114892/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a66baea-5fb6-50af-a550-e2605aa07c9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114892/selection/f7c1bd5baf2cded1aba0b23d3926e4ee550542bfbe6822146aeca77be444a09f" :answer-field/choices ["q-114892/selection/d6ac097fc4be373c41b4c0395ed665d7e57a175ad636bf8133302d28472ae4b4" "q-114892/selection/bfb95ea717d59358860f0615a38c5a1c60c502b49272d182b54768de605d975b" "q-114892/selection/0bdb3932af7cd815b3772b59b683586b1d77a12e90bdba358128ae83aa0ae167" "q-114892/selection/29c33bfd6d1591d14ddbf2aba437b23e0305d7be3e8226d3b2fad41ffcbdeea8" "q-114892/selection/f7c1bd5baf2cded1aba0b23d3926e4ee550542bfbe6822146aeca77be444a09f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114892" :question/id #uuid "0a47a19d-1921-5357-895e-fb0a72629e4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-114892" :question/problem "${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2(x+\\frac{3}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & 3 & -4 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & 3 & -\\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x-4}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})} & =3-\\frac{(\\frac{17}{2})}{(x+\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{17}{2(x+\\frac{3}{2})} \\\\  & =3-\\frac{17}{2x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{3x-4}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3-\\frac{17}{2x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[3{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-17{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[3x-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+3|]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[3(2-0)-\\frac{17}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2(2)+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2(0)+3|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[6-\\frac{17}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[6-\\frac{17}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3})] \\\\  & =3-\\frac{17}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{7}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-114892/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114892"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73392/selection/7a056db6a784b282efd1da0af0c5d048b95e1d4c39b922b89edfb2d5073b15af" :answer/id #uuid "253e0e12-fbaf-5a39-bbfb-820fa13b60d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73392/selection/35988736d34fa4ad37835d1b23d7354f837dcd65596d8633d3ad8b40e450c8cc" :answer/id #uuid "00bf9bab-e697-5c8f-b378-0ddca2be3fac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73392/selection/2e893395eed651992d391594c42d2b41b56741db9aad359faf43a4730d55845a" :answer/id #uuid "f6fa9517-0bf4-5c5d-b3b9-6dd7502a3d13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73392/selection/257b7f79f6b054b6ecb74c85112754804a3b2183bb3e031dcf706da4a566fc9f" :answer/id #uuid "838ede82-8ed2-5ef1-aef1-e164c6498a7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73392/selection/bcd6d7a3107556d5df8c59c255fbb5b9fecde0a8c78026203e314412abd51cbe" :answer/id #uuid "1a5d29a7-90d0-55b6-b519-45be6629db78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73392/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a91b7c95-ab58-55b4-a6a1-00c0e9da230f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73392/selection/2e893395eed651992d391594c42d2b41b56741db9aad359faf43a4730d55845a" :answer-field/choices ["q-73392/selection/7a056db6a784b282efd1da0af0c5d048b95e1d4c39b922b89edfb2d5073b15af" "q-73392/selection/35988736d34fa4ad37835d1b23d7354f837dcd65596d8633d3ad8b40e450c8cc" "q-73392/selection/2e893395eed651992d391594c42d2b41b56741db9aad359faf43a4730d55845a" "q-73392/selection/257b7f79f6b054b6ecb74c85112754804a3b2183bb3e031dcf706da4a566fc9f" "q-73392/selection/bcd6d7a3107556d5df8c59c255fbb5b9fecde0a8c78026203e314412abd51cbe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73392" :question/id #uuid "81a5f9d4-4d33-54e5-b177-b660410e589f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73392" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x+6}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x+6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x-1}{2(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{(x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 1 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 \\\\  & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{(x+3)} & =1+\\frac{(-4)}{(x+3)} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{4}{(x+3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x+6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\frac{4}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\int \\text{d}x-4\\int \\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73392/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73392"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73391/selection/a3030e6210aeb3f6494ecb72b6aacc12c5c32af80a3a065dd86460e6fa2bf656" :answer/id #uuid "06f32f5a-d56c-5081-84b4-dca0e328942e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73391/selection/621565692bc19b4ae1119762feeefc713725d718b24ea92548439d801e9ba513" :answer/id #uuid "c8ede3df-b267-5dc0-8d33-5cf94aec0675" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73391/selection/451c74c0bf840b12e1f4206e97fa25c170047ef24c7bff6b6a0b44e340f817f3" :answer/id #uuid "a31a2406-8c00-544b-b546-9fb5a6cb8839" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73391/selection/b33fc541641eca42e32602f344661ac692225431c8bfa82044e4c324ad3379b3" :answer/id #uuid "d3f2d779-8c3a-54e5-81ce-1ea0aabe1568" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73391/selection/c08f80cc0b115693fc8b6ab697ce5c1cf8e89c337c4c4c88bc03da85f5c42342" :answer/id #uuid "d19b9b0e-b55f-5ab1-82ad-89e1f137dde2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x+9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73391/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf83b17d-180d-56c4-973a-30baa98fb981" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73391/selection/b33fc541641eca42e32602f344661ac692225431c8bfa82044e4c324ad3379b3" :answer-field/choices ["q-73391/selection/a3030e6210aeb3f6494ecb72b6aacc12c5c32af80a3a065dd86460e6fa2bf656" "q-73391/selection/621565692bc19b4ae1119762feeefc713725d718b24ea92548439d801e9ba513" "q-73391/selection/451c74c0bf840b12e1f4206e97fa25c170047ef24c7bff6b6a0b44e340f817f3" "q-73391/selection/b33fc541641eca42e32602f344661ac692225431c8bfa82044e4c324ad3379b3" "q-73391/selection/c08f80cc0b115693fc8b6ab697ce5c1cf8e89c337c4c4c88bc03da85f5c42342"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73391" :question/id #uuid "5f43a9f2-6f72-5d1e-8a03-5c7d7f915857" :question/math-academy-id "q-73391" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{x-1}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $3$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x-1}{3(x-\\frac{2}{3})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{2}{3})}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & 1 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & 1 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{2}{3})} & =1+\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{3})}{(x-\\frac{2}{3})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{3(x-\\frac{2}{3})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{3x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int (1-\\frac{1}{3x-2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\int \\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[x-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73391/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73391"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114898/selection/18e8ba9607ceef5e23242020ad3381113909ac32d8ad846f35f6fc9a7e605392" :answer/id #uuid "221c19cb-0523-57d0-b722-73c15d635554" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114898/selection/90ab48dff9fab96b810fd7f0fd456c3d4e0462429f6f1e123d55669ec55a0001" :answer/id #uuid "07d23c95-2369-5cbf-8fbc-7e0bd7387b68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114898/selection/d31b28536b262fb3b83393f6bd907391c19d788819eb5d77e415afd61b2810a5" :answer/id #uuid "703b2b05-c249-5636-a9c7-abdc4bc16f73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114898/selection/e4f3c659ae1e1e6e5f43337d7da57a4998a8209aa869d385f33791059a959919" :answer/id #uuid "e3da8ac1-dd09-5222-9142-60c214c5338a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}[2-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114898/selection/0a7222b954d8d2ad7b1441c6f541a36ae9b699e5ed62be266ea5eea8defad90c" :answer/id #uuid "0948f21f-5869-5563-81ca-a8ca27a6796c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}[1-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114898/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ee1680ad-2ab3-5ea4-b389-42d35cfcf513" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114898/selection/0a7222b954d8d2ad7b1441c6f541a36ae9b699e5ed62be266ea5eea8defad90c" :answer-field/choices ["q-114898/selection/18e8ba9607ceef5e23242020ad3381113909ac32d8ad846f35f6fc9a7e605392" "q-114898/selection/90ab48dff9fab96b810fd7f0fd456c3d4e0462429f6f1e123d55669ec55a0001" "q-114898/selection/d31b28536b262fb3b83393f6bd907391c19d788819eb5d77e415afd61b2810a5" "q-114898/selection/e4f3c659ae1e1e6e5f43337d7da57a4998a8209aa869d385f33791059a959919" "q-114898/selection/0a7222b954d8d2ad7b1441c6f541a36ae9b699e5ed62be266ea5eea8defad90c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114898" :question/id #uuid "349a53dd-d24d-57f8-9b3f-ad7d5c48d97a" :question/math-academy-id "q-114898" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $4$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4(x-\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{(x-\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & 8 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & 2 \\\\  & 8 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x+1}{(x-\\frac{1}{4})} & =8+\\frac{3}{(x-\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =8+\\frac{12}{4x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{8x+1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}(8+\\frac{12}{4x-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\text{d}x+12{\\int }_{-1/8}^{0}\\frac{1}{4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8x+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x-1|]_{-1/8}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8(0-(-\\frac{1}{8}))+3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4(0)-1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4(-\\frac{1}{8})-1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8(\\frac{1}{8})+3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[1-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2})].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-114898/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114898"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-49467"] :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{2(x+\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $5$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-\\frac{5}{2}$ |\n|  | $5$ | $-\\frac{7}{2}$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-1}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})} & =5-\\frac{(\\frac{7}{2})}{(x+\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =5-\\frac{7}{2(x+\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =5-\\frac{7}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{5x-1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(5-\\frac{7}{2x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-7{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5x{|}_{0}^{2}-\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|{|}_{0}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5(2-0)-\\frac{7}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2\\cdot 2+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2\\cdot 0+1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[10-\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5] \\\\  & =5-\\frac{7}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-485"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 \\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}-1$ | $4$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1} = 4 -\\dfrac{5}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4-\\frac{5}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x{|}_{0}^{1}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[4-0]-5[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1] \\\\  & =4-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-486"] :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{2x^2-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division. \n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^2$ | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}3$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n|  | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{ 2x^2-3x-4}{x-3} = 2x + 3 + \\dfrac {5}{x-3} .\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+3+\\frac{5}{x-3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+3x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-487"] :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x-1}{2(x-\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}\\dfrac12$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $\\dfrac12$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-\\dfrac12$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} & =1-\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\frac{1}{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
